{"abstract":[{"text":"Boot a game, feed it the commands a player would type, and assert on what it printed.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Gnusto game is a value and a play session is a function of its typed input, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the natural test is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"transcript test","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" boots"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the game, feeds it a list of commands, and returns everything printed with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input interleaved as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"> command"},{"type":"text","text":" — the same text the player saw. Everything else"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in this library either cuts that string down to the part a claim is about, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records a Swift Testing issue with the whole of it attached, which is what a bare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(transcript.contains(…))"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot do. Gnusto’s own suite is roughly a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thousand tests of this shape."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is neither a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle nor a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GamePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". It declares no verbs,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no rules and no entities, and a game never links it: it is a test-only helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library, and it imports the toolchain’s Testing library, which ships with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiler rather than the OS. Put it in a test target’s dependencies and nowhere"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else — an executable that links it can fail at load time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host passes a game type and a list of commands; the library holds one piece"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of state of its own, a process-wide cache of prepared games behind a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mutex"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" exists because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bootstrap.build"},{"type":"text","text":" reflects"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over the game and every content bundle it lists, and that runs about 15× longer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a turn does. The suite boots the same handful of game types thousands of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times, so building each once and copying the prepared definition takes bootstrap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out of the suite’s critical path. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"play"},{"type":"text","text":" goes through it; a test that wants the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"world rather than the transcript can call it directly and drive "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"REPL"},{"type":"text","text":" itself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Gnusto catalog’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Testing Your Game","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" article teaches four of these helpers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the habits around them — pinning a seed, sweeping "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GNUSTO_SEED"},{"type":"text","text":" for tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that pass by luck, deciding when a trap is worth a test at all. This page is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list it stops short of."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"A-transcript-test","text":"A transcript test"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","@Test func ringingTheBellWinsTheGame() async throws {","    let transcript = try await play(","        MyGame(),","        [\"take rope\", \"north\", \"ring bell\"],","        seed: 7)","","    expectInOrder(","        transcript,","        [","            \"Village Garden\",","            \"Taken.\",","            \"Bell Tower\",","            \"The great bronze bell peals\",","        ])","","    let looking = turnOutput(of: \"examine hook\", in: transcript)","    #expect(looking.contains(\"screwed to the wall\"))","    #expect(occurrences(of: \"The bell tolls\", in: transcript) == 1)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Omit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seed:"},{"type":"text","text":" and the stream is fresh each run, unless "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GNUSTO_SEED"},{"type":"text","text":" is set,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which pins every call that passed no seed of its own and leaves the ones that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"did alone. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"saveDirectory:"},{"type":"text","text":" when a test exercises named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"save"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so it never writes to the real per-user saves directory."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Slicing-before-asserting","text":"Slicing before asserting"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"turnOutput(of:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" matches the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" occurrence of a command, so a route"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that types "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"look"},{"type":"text","text":" four times wants four different commands or a different"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"helper. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"output(after:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"output(before:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" cut on any marker rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a prompt, which is the slice for “and then, later…”. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"occurrences(of:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the count assertion — a beat that must fire exactly once."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lines(mentioning:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the matching lines in transcript order, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what an alignment check compares between two runs to prove that a guard burned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no randomness."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Asserting","text":"Asserting"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectInOrder"},{"type":"text","text":" is the workhorse: a sequence of substrings, each match resuming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after the last, strict enough to pin the beats that matter and loose enough to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"survive an edit between them. The rest of the assertions are about a whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript rather than a phrase in it. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectEveryNounAnswered"},{"type":"text","text":" fails on either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answer a game gives a noun it doesn’t know — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"I don't know the word \"x\""},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"You can't see any such thing"},{"type":"text","text":" — which is what a walk of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x <noun>"},{"type":"text","text":" over a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"room’s own description is checking. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectNoAmbiguity"},{"type":"text","text":" fails on "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Which do you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mean…","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", and is deliberately a separate call: an unanswered noun is always a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"defect, while an ambiguity is only one where the author believed the room held a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single thing of that kind."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives"},{"type":"text","text":" is for a game that has re-voiced the stub verbs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and wants to keep the claim whole. It reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text.stubs"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mirror"},{"type":"text","text":" rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than naming the properties, so a stub added to the engine tomorrow is compared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the day it lands. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"engineVoicedStubLines"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same sweep without the issue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recording, split out so the sweep itself can be tested for being alive — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection loop that matches nothing passes silently."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","text":"Trapping a `fatalError`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The engine answers an authoring mistake by crashing with a message that names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fatalError"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be caught, so the only way to assert on one is to run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it in a child process and read what it printed; Swift Testing’s exit tests do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the running and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectTrap"},{"type":"text","text":" does the reading."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let result = await #expect(processExitsWith: .failure, observing: [\\.standardErrorContent]) {","    _ = try await play(MyGame(), [\"prime the bomb\"])","}","expectTrap(result, says: \"names a daemon\", \"use startDaemon(_:)\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call is a child process, some 60 ms against 1 ms for an in-process"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"assertion, and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":" has to stay at the call site because its body is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiled into a C function that captures nothing. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectTrap"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own doc comment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carries the rule for when that is worth spending, since it is where the person"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deciding is standing: make the bad message unrepresentable and write no test,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or split the message into a pure function and assert it in a millisecond, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaching for the third shape. Exit tests are built on macOS, Linux and Windows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and are absent elsewhere, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectTrap"},{"type":"text","text":" is compiled under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GNUSTO_EXIT_TESTS"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a test using it wants a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if"},{"type":"text","text":" on a suite that also runs on iOS, watchOS,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tvOS, visionOS or WASI."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"GnustoTestSupport","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"GnustoTestSupport","modules":[{"name":"GnustoTestSupport"}]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Playing a session","anchor":"Playing-a-session","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(after:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(before:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)"],"anchor":"Slicing-a-transcript","title":"Slicing a transcript"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/engineVoicedStubLines(in:)"],"anchor":"Asserting","title":"Asserting"},{"title":"Trapping a `fatalError`","anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)"]},{"title":"Functions","anchor":"Functions","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoStockRefusal(_:_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/frame(headed:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(afterLast:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/stockFragment(of:)"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/stockFragment(of:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part of a stock line no subject can vary — the engine’s own wording,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the noun taken out."}],"title":"stockFragment(of:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stockFragment","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9StockLineP","text":"StockLine","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/stockFragment(of:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/stockfragment(of:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/occurrences(of:in:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"occurrences"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sy","text":"StringProtocol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How many times "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"needle"},{"type":"text","text":" occurs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"haystack"},{"type":"text","text":" — the count assertions in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript tests are usually about (“this beat fires exactly once”)."}],"title":"occurrences(of:in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/expectinorder(_:_:sourcelocation:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)","title":"expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records one Swift Testing issue (at the caller’s source location) if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"needles do not appear in the transcript in the given order; each match"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resumes searching after the previous one. On failure the full transcript"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is included in the issue message."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"expectInOrder"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SourceLocation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/play(_:_:seed:savedirectory:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"play"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4GameP","text":"Game"},{"kind":"text","text":", ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"seed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UInt64","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt64V"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"saveDirectory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Boots a game, feeds it a list of commands, and returns the full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript — every line the game printed, with the player’s input"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interleaved as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"> command"},{"type":"text","text":" the way a player would see it."}],"title":"play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport","title":"GnustoTestSupport","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Boot a game, feed it the commands a player would type, and assert on what it printed."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/expectnoambiguity(_:_:sourcelocation:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","title":"expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a Swift Testing issue if the transcript contains a disambiguation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"question — "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Which do you mean: the narrow chimney or the small door?”"}]}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"expectNoAmbiguity"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SourceLocation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/lines(mentioning:in:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lines"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"mentioning"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lines of a transcript slice that mention "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"needle"},{"type":"text","text":", in order."}],"title":"lines(mentioning:in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/output(afterLast:in:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/output(afterlast:in:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"output(afterLast:in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(afterLast:in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything a transcript printed after its "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"last"}]},{"type":"text","text":" occurrence of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"marker"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"output"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"afterLast"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","pre